<Layout title="Employment measures for aid beneficiaries | Spain 2026" description="Practical overview of Article 36 of Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 and its possible impact on certain employment decisions.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Legal updates · Business" title="Employment measures for certain companies receiving direct aid" description="What Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 changes and what a company should check before a sensitive employment decision." primaryLabel="Review our company situation" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Back to legal updates" secondaryHref="/en/legal-updates" note="Published: 30 September 2026 · Effective: 1 October 2026 · Primary source: BOE." />
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>What changes and until when</h2><p>Until 31 December 2026, Article 36 of Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 prevents certain companies receiving direct aid from dismissing workers for force majeure or economic, technical, organisational or production reasons arising from the situation addressed by the law.</p><h2>Who may be affected</h2><p>It does not apply to every company or every dismissal. The company must have received one of the specified forms of direct aid, and the reason for the decision must have the connection required by the law. For permanent seasonal contracts, the article also addresses ending an activity period or failing to call a worker back.</p><p>A breach may require repayment of the aid and result in the dismissal being treated as null. Its application needs to be checked against the official wording and the facts.</p><p><a href="https://www.boe.es/buscar/act.php?id=BOE-A-2026-20265" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 at the BOE →</a></p></div></section><CTA title="Does this affect your company?" text="We can review the aid, the proposed measure and the documents before a decision is implemented." label="Contact the firm" /></Layout>
